{
  "_comment": [
    "Ranged gear that wears a metal prefix but is not gated on the melee metal ladder.",
    "'nouns' maps the last word of a cleaned card name to a family; both spellings are",
    "listed because the game uses one of each ('Bronze bolts' plural, 'Rune arrow'",
    "singular) and no stemmer turns 'knives' into 'knife'.",
    "'families' gives the Ranged level each metal really needs. A metal with no item in",
    "the family is simply absent (there is no black arrow) and the caller falls back to",
    "the tier ladder's own number. Ammunition carries no equip requirement at all, so",
    "the number encoded is the LAUNCHER's - a yew bow (40) for rune arrows, an adamant",
    "crossbow (46) for adamant bolts."
  ],
